# p5 mcp: a stdio server that writes to stderr and exits 3 at every start is
# `retrying` -- which the status line never names -- until its eighth try in a
# row fails, about 91 s after launch (fx v0.0.16's engine: eight tries, the
# backoffs 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 30 and 30 s), and is then `bad failed · /mcp`; a
# prompt sent clears it. No project server and no menu: the whole screen is
# the status line's (MCP-S).
# The stdio server is p5-mcp-stdio.ts, which the profile names by `@BUN@` and
# `@SCENARIOS@` (capture.sh writes both in), and xfx is given the same profile.
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-fail-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-fail-profile.json
gateway p5-mcp-hello.json
wait 13
snap retrying
wait 71
snap still-retrying
wait 16
snap failed
type hello
key Enter
wait 4
snap after-prompt
